{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0735", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$g : (\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C})\n\\to (\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D})$", "MATH_0002": "$g^* : \\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D}) \\to\n\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0003": "$$\ng^* : D(\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D}) \\to D(\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C})\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$D(\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D})$", "MATH_0005": "$g^*$", "MATH_0006": "$Lg^*$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-base-change}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-flat-pullback-exact}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{derived-lemma-right-derived-exact-functor}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:386caa43463298ba7935acd7bd5aa6cbfc4813287862c1bbcf75328addf7ec66", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cf8a731cd0b8f2c7d7fd949a60710cfe6ea35c06442a20b75577b101c7215468", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we construct the base change map in some cases;\nthe general case is treated in Remark <REF_0001>.\nThe discussion in this section avoids using\nderived pullback by restricting to the case of a base change\nby a flat morphism of ringed sites.\nBefore we state the result, let us discuss flat pullback on the derived\ncategory. Suppose\n<MATH_0001>\nis a flat morphism of ringed topoi. By\nModules on Sites, Lemma <REF_0002>\nthe functor <MATH_0002> is exact.\nHence it has a derived functor\n<MATH_0003>\nwhich is computed by simply pulling back an representative of a given\nobject in <MATH_0004>, see\nDerived Categories, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nIt preserved the bounded (above, below) subcategories.\nHence as indicated we indicate this functor by <MATH_0005> rather than <MATH_0006>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8bc62f3efacf3d12f1d6a3390bc22379037c5384c57d354f2eaa953027001db5", "unit_id": "tag:0735:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0735", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}'), \\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{C}'})\n\\ar[r]_{g'} \\ar[d]_{f'} &\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}) \\ar[d]^f \\\\\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}'), \\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{D}'})\n\\ar[r]^g &\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D})\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$g$", "MATH_0005": "$g'$", "MATH_0006": "$$\ng^*Rf_*\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet\n\\longrightarrow\nR(f')_*(g')^*\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$D^{+}(\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{D}'})$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-base-change-map-flat-case}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5ba5f6d81a5ca13fc6fa685fd8b8f67b841e832d379bdf609873b23d6905caec", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b6af514996ec01fa68632fe6513a58206402459ee3b3d49a29839740f75948a7", "source_text": "Let\n<MATH_0001>\nbe a commutative diagram of ringed topoi.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a bounded below complex of\n<MATH_0003>-modules.\nAssume both <MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005> are flat.\nThen there exists a canonical base change map\n<MATH_0006>\nin <MATH_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:558605094914bd3e6a984e5e07acb49d8261f583e1fff1f886f9c0987f678e3d", "unit_id": "tag:0736:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0735", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet \\to \\mathcal{I}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0002": "$(g')^*\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet \\to \\mathcal{J}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0003": "$(g')_*\\mathcal{J}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0004": "$R(g')_*(g')^*\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0005": "$\\beta$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n(g')_*(g')^*\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet \\ar[r] &\n(g')_*\\mathcal{J}^\\bullet \\\\\n\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet \\ar[u]^{adjunction} \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet \\ar[u]_\\beta\n}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0008": "$$\nf_*\\beta :\nf_*\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet\n\\longrightarrow\nf_*(g')_*\\mathcal{J}^\\bullet\n=\ng_*(f')_*\\mathcal{J}^\\bullet\n$$", "MATH_0009": "$g^*$", "MATH_0010": "$g_*$", "MATH_0011": "$g^*f_*\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet \\to (f')_*\\mathcal{J}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0012": "$\\beta$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-pushforward-injective-flat}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{derived-lemma-morphisms-lift}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{derived-lemma-morphisms-equal-up-to-homotopy}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f2439ff991750ff39ed34fa01026ccd70ab7b654b1449d27198ed32a9ecb779b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5abb1c5bd6727cc606c962818b0e9770011a9c7dfe9fcb31badcb314b18383a5", "source_text": "Choose injective resolutions <MATH_0001>\nand <MATH_0002>.\nBy Lemma <REF_0001> we see that\n<MATH_0003> is a complex of injectives representing\n<MATH_0004>. Hence by\nDerived Categories, Lemmas <REF_0002>\nand <REF_0003>\nthe arrow <MATH_0005> in the diagram\n<MATH_0006>\nexists and is unique up to homotopy.\nPushing down to <MATH_0007> we get\n<MATH_0008>\nBy adjunction of <MATH_0009> and <MATH_0010> we get a map of complexes\n<MATH_0011>.\nNote that this map is unique up to homotopy since the only\nchoice in the whole process was the choice of the map <MATH_0012>\nand everything was done on the level of complexes.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:339cf03169a9102647b75e5495e86537d081e138623f8a3dcfdc6a4184aa5b91", "unit_id": "tag:0736:proof"}
